Article 2 (Missions)
The Drone Operations Command (hereinafter referred to as the "Command") shall perform the following missions:
1. Planning and execution of the following military operations using drone forces (hereinafter referred to as "drone operations"):
(a) Military operations, including detection, tracking and strikes, to respond to enemy unmanned aircraft [unreadable source characters appear between the expressions for "response to" and "detection, tracking and strikes"; legal source restoration required];
(b) Military operations involving strategic and operational surveillance and reconnaissance, strikes, psychological operations and electromagnetic operations;
2. Development of combat capabilities for drone operations;
3. Other matters relating to drone operations.
